  "decision": "Two opposing-order pairs are exploratory evidence. They can leave performance admission unproven but do not alone establish that code caused either improvement or regression. Require repeated complete workloads and mechanistic evidence; keep correctness,capacity failure and physical reclamation evidence distinct.",
  "alternatives_considered": [
    "Treat every observed slowdown as causal: rejected because identical artifacts also vary.",
    "Treat a percentage derived from this one null control as universal noise threshold: rejected; sample small,environment and workload specific.",
    "Admit unproven candidates because variation exists: rejected; correctness and reproducible end-to-end benefit still required."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Eight same-artifact runs on one host; no confidence interval or universal acceptance threshold.",
    "A null control does not establish equivalence or performance admission of any candidate.",
    "Prior actual range-witness failures and validated online reclamation remain direct evidence.",
    "No SQLite comparison,provider/browser/full-soak evidence or all-scenario superiority claim."
  ],
